WEBVTT

asr-000143
01:07:18.760 --> 01:07:30.000
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I apologize for the delay. I know we should have started at around three, but we had to go to the session hall because I had to sponsor several measures before the floor.

asr-000144
01:07:30.000 --> 01:07:59.980
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So I do apologize and thank you for your patience and understanding. Well, let us now begin. Magandang hapon po sa ating lahat. The budget briefing for fiscal year 2007 proposed budgets of the Commission on Filipinos Overseas and the Philippine Reclamation Authority is hereby called to order. We will be joined by several of our colleagues later on.

asr-000145
01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:23.900
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I would also like to thank and acknowledge the presence of CFO Secretary Dante Ang and PRA Chairman Alexander Lopez. At this juncture, may I ask the Committee Secretary to acknowledge our other resource persons in today's budget briefing?

asr-000145-split-2
01:08:23.900 --> 01:08:31.120
Committee Secretary: Yes, thank you, Mr. Chair. The Committee on Finance, Subcommittee H, would like to acknowledge the presence of the following:

asr-000146
01:08:31.120 --> 01:08:59.980
Committee Secretary: From the Commission on Filipinos Overseas, earlier acknowledged by the Chairman, we have Secretary Dante Francis Ang II. Good afternoon po. We also have Undersecretary Maria [unclear] Borja. From the Philippine Reclamation Authority, also earlier acknowledged by Chairman Senator Erwin Tulfo:

asr-000147
01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:29.980
Committee Secretary: Attorney Alexander Lopez, Engineer Cesar Siador Jr., Director Elio [unclear], Director Anthony Peter Crisologo, Attorney Jose Ferrer Jr., and Attorney Joselito Gonzalez.

asr-000148
01:09:30.000 --> 01:09:40.000
Committee Secretary: Attorney Joseph John [unclear]. From the Commission on Audit for the Commission on Filipinos Overseas,

asr-000158
01:09:40.000 --> 01:09:50.000
Committee Secretary: we have Mr. Fahad bin Abdul Malik Tumawis.

asr-000168
01:09:50.000 --> 01:09:51.000
Committee Secretary: From the Commission on Audit for the Philippine Reclamation Authority, we have Mr. Marlon Marcadia. Good afternoon, sir.

asr-000177
01:09:59.000 --> 01:10:08.200
Committee Secretary: From the Department of Budget and Management for Commission on Filipinas Overseas, we have Ms. Mary Rose Aguilar, good afternoon ma'am.

asr-000178
01:10:09.200 --> 01:10:18.520
Committee Secretary: And also from the Department of Budget and Management for Philippine Reclamation Authority, we have Ms. Lulu Vizpo, good afternoon po.

asr-000179
01:10:19.160 --> 01:10:21.060
Committee Secretary: I think that is all, Mr. Chair.

asr-000180
01:10:21.060 --> 01:10:32.700
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you, Committee Secretary. I would like to acknowledge the presence of our Minority Leader, Senator Alan Peter Cayetano. Thank you, sir, for joining us this afternoon.

asr-000181
01:10:33.820 --> 01:10:47.760
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Anyway, for today, the Finance Subcommittee H will deliberate on the fiscal year 2027 proposed budgets of the Commission on Filipinos Overseas and the Philippine Reclamation Authority.

asr-000182
01:10:47.760 --> 01:10:50.660
Senator Erwin Tulfo: As we deliberate on the 2027 budget,

asr-000183
01:10:51.060 --> 01:10:57.380
Senator Erwin Tulfo: let us remember that every peso appropriated is a peso entrusted to us by the people.

asr-000184
01:10:58.040 --> 01:11:04.620
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kaya dapat malinaw po saan napupunta ang ating pondo, ano ang resulta, at sino ang tunay na makikinabang.

asr-000185
01:11:05.320 --> 01:11:08.100
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For the CFO, our starting point is equally clear.

asr-000186
01:11:08.760 --> 01:11:11.820
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Hindi lamang remittance ang ambag ng ating mga kababayan sa abroad.

asr-000187
01:11:12.380 --> 01:11:19.240
Senator Erwin Tulfo: They bring skills, investments, ideas, networks, and most importantly, a continuing connection to the Philippines.

asr-000188
01:11:20.240 --> 01:11:20.820
Senator Erwin Tulfo: For the PRA,

asr-000189
01:11:21.060 --> 01:11:26.520
Senator Erwin Tulfo: we will look closely at the balance between development and environmental stewardship.

asr-000190
01:11:27.300 --> 01:11:32.220
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Reclamation and the development of public lands must be anchored on sound planning,

asr-000191
01:11:33.500 --> 01:11:38.420
Senator Erwin Tulfo: economic value, climate resilience, and the long-term interests of Filipino people.

asr-000192
01:11:39.180 --> 01:11:40.640
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Hindi po sapat na may proyekto.

asr-000193
01:11:41.280 --> 01:11:45.040
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Dapat malinaw kung may tunay na pakinabang sa publiko.

asr-000194
01:11:50.180 --> 01:11:51.040
Senator Erwin Tulfo: At the end of this deliberation,

asr-000195
01:11:51.060 --> 01:11:52.720
Senator Erwin Tulfo: our standards should be clear:

asr-000196
01:11:53.060 --> 01:11:58.500
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Translate into public value, measurable results, and meaningful services to the Filipino people.

asr-000197
01:11:59.000 --> 01:12:05.720
Senator Erwin Tulfo: This is how we uphold fiscal responsibility and more importantly, maintain the trust that our people place in government.

asr-000198
01:12:06.500 --> 01:12:11.700
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Let this hearing therefore be candid, constructive, and focused on the outcomes.

asr-000199
01:12:12.300 --> 01:12:14.400
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ang budget ay hindi lamang po numero sa papel.

asr-000200
01:12:15.140 --> 01:12:19.380
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ito ay salamin ng ating mga prioridad at pananagutan sa mamamayan.

asr-000201
01:12:19.380 --> 01:12:20.540
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you.

asr-000202
01:12:21.060 --> 01:12:21.780
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Let's proceed.

asr-000203
01:12:21.880 --> 01:12:22.860
Senator Erwin Tulfo: But before we do that,

asr-000204
01:12:23.400 --> 01:12:29.940
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I would like to ask our minority leader, Senator Cayetano, if he has any opening statement.

asr-000205
01:12:30.440 --> 01:12:32.040
Senator Alan Peter S. Cayetano: Thank you very much, Mr. Chairman.

asr-000206
01:12:32.340 --> 01:12:33.580
Senator Alan Peter S. Cayetano: I will follow your lead.

asr-000207
01:12:34.260 --> 01:12:39.300
Senator Alan Peter S. Cayetano: You said to keep it clear, focused, professional.

asr-000208
01:12:40.260 --> 01:12:46.060
Senator Alan Peter S. Cayetano: So, sa akin lang po yung biblical principle, kung anong ating itatanim, yan ang ating aanihin.

asr-000209
01:12:46.060 --> 01:12:51.060
Senator Alan Peter S. Cayetano: And in that spirit, after the chairman, may I ask one or two questions?

asr-000210
01:12:51.060 --> 01:12:55.560
Senator Alan Peter S. Cayetano: To the Honourable Secretary Dante, about Filipinos overseas.

asr-000211
01:12:56.880 --> 01:12:58.460
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you, Mayor.

asr-000212
01:12:59.720 --> 01:13:04.120
Senator Erwin Tulfo: With that, let us proceed with our budget hearing.

asr-000213
01:13:04.840 --> 01:13:12.920
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We will open the floor now for the Commission on Filipinos Overseas, if they have any or if they want to make any presentation.

asr-000214
01:13:13.740 --> 01:13:14.880
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Secretary Ang, go ahead.

asr-000215
01:13:16.980 --> 01:13:19.560
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: Good afternoon, Mr. Chair, Honourable Members of the Committee.

asr-000216
01:13:19.560 --> 01:13:20.980
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: With your permission.

asr-000217
01:13:21.060 --> 01:13:26.880
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: Sirs, I have a two-page opening statement and a five-minute video, if that would be okay.

asr-000218
01:13:28.300 --> 01:13:28.700
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Go ahead.

asr-000219
01:13:28.940 --> 01:13:29.460
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: Salamat po.

asr-000220
01:13:30.020 --> 01:13:39.120
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: Whenever stakeholders hear us, it is often followed by questions about our connection to our other migrant-serving counterparts and our scope of work.

asr-000221
01:13:40.120 --> 01:13:47.340
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: Put simply, the CFO's mandate is to foster diaspora engagement through programs and policies

asr-000222
01:13:47.760 --> 01:13:50.640
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: that involve and empower our non-resident Filipinos.

asr-000223
01:13:51.060 --> 01:13:54.680
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: To participate in national development.

asr-000224
01:13:55.740 --> 01:14:09.140
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: NRF is our term for permanent migrants, expatriates, dual citizens, marriage migrants, as well as all their descendants and cultural exchange program participants in the U.S. and Europe.

asr-000225
01:14:10.360 --> 01:14:20.300
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: They are the reason why the CFO exists under Batas Pambansa 79 to serve migrating Filipinos and lead in the Brain Gain initiatives.

asr-000226
01:14:21.060 --> 01:14:27.860
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: The CFO ensures that NRFs are connected to the Philippines politically, economically, and culturally.

asr-000227
01:14:28.480 --> 01:14:31.780
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: The Philippines enjoys a competitive advantage.

asr-000228
01:14:32.700 --> 01:14:38.100
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: But Filipinos overseas need programs and policies that enable them to participate in development.

asr-000229
01:14:38.980 --> 01:14:43.220
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: First, the CFO serves the largest segment of our migrants.

asr-000230
01:14:43.220 --> 01:14:51.000
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: About 60% of the estimated 10.7 million Filipinos residing overseas fall under the CFO's

asr-000231
01:14:51.060 --> 01:14:54.340
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: specific purview and require government services.

asr-000232
01:14:54.980 --> 01:15:00.020
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: This is more than half of the population, and they are vital resources for the Philippines.

asr-000233
01:15:00.000 --> 01:15:08.240
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: The diaspora, despite migrating long-term, continues to identify with being Filipino

asr-000234
01:15:08.240 --> 01:15:14.640
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: and expresses an earnest desire to be involved in the country. Second is its economic significance.

asr-000235
01:15:15.440 --> 01:15:22.640
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: just like ofws our nrfs bring in a significant amount of remittances but they are hardly

asr-000236
01:15:22.640 --> 01:15:28.560
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: recognized for this contribution. Our flagship diaspora program, Lingkod sa Kapwa Pilipino (LINKAPIL),

asr-000237
01:15:30.320 --> 01:15:35.920
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: has facilitated more than 3.4 billion pesos in contributions over the decades.

asr-000238
01:15:36.800 --> 01:15:41.840
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: in relation the cfo's constituents not only give back economically as the chairman said

asr-000239
01:15:42.400 --> 01:15:45.600
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: but they also provide knowledge and skills transfer to communities

asr-000240
01:15:46.320 --> 01:15:50.800
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: we have done medical mission they have done medical missions capacity building workshops

asr-000241
01:15:50.800 --> 01:15:52.560
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: and consultations with our partners

asr-000242
01:15:53.280 --> 01:15:58.480
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: The LINKAPIL economic engagement program is one through which NRFs can help SMEs in

asr-000243
01:15:58.480 --> 01:16:04.080
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: the philippines and support small-scale infrastructure third is harnessing political

asr-000244
01:16:04.080 --> 01:16:10.320
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: and social capital. Our NRFs serve as informal ambassadors of our country,

asr-000245
01:16:10.320 --> 01:16:16.800
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: imbued with soft power some diaspora members are not only community leaders but they also

asr-000246
01:16:16.800 --> 01:16:22.400
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: serve in key positions in governments overseas the cfo collaborates with these important

asr-000247
01:16:22.400 --> 01:16:22.560
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: figures

asr-000248
01:16:22.640 --> 01:16:27.440
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: and opens the way for business, social, and tourism ventures in the Philippines.

asr-000249
01:16:28.320 --> 01:16:34.720
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: the creation of the cfo in 1980 signaled a clear recognition that international migration

asr-000250
01:16:34.720 --> 01:16:40.080
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: extended beyond labor mobility and required focused attention on immigrant populations

asr-000251
01:16:40.080 --> 01:16:46.640
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: and transnational engagement our filipino diaspora summit last june brought together

asr-000252
01:16:46.640 --> 01:16:52.400
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: nrfs from around the world and echoed the same sentiment it proved that the diaspora

asr-000253
01:16:52.400 --> 01:16:57.920
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: is not seeking engagement the philippines in the abstract but rather with specific concrete

asr-000254
01:16:57.920 --> 01:17:04.960
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: development opportunities provided by the cfo thus it are it is our intention to continue our mission

asr-000255
01:17:04.960 --> 01:17:09.360
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: and ensure that the contributions welfare and interests of our permanent and long-term

asr-000256
01:17:09.360 --> 01:17:19.280
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: migrants are not neglected. To facilitate our plans, the CFO is proposing a budget of 195.2 million pesos. Forty-eight percent,

asr-000257
01:17:20.720 --> 01:17:22.080
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: or 93.898 million pesos,

asr-000258
01:17:22.400 --> 01:17:30.720
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: will be allocated to personnel services, while 52 percent, or 101.302 million pesos,

asr-000259
01:17:30.720 --> 01:17:34.720
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: will be allocated for maintenance and other operating expenses, or MOOE.

asr-000260
01:17:35.520 --> 01:17:38.800
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: in terms of distribution by major program activity or project

asr-000261
01:17:39.600 --> 01:17:44.800
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: 73.26 million will be allocated to general administration and support or gas

asr-000262
01:17:46.160 --> 01:17:52.320
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: the cfo assures that the budget shall be maximized to its fullest potential as evidenced by a previous

asr-000263
01:17:52.400 --> 01:18:00.080
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: performance in 2025 we were able to obligate 91.36 percent of our of our budget with a

asr-000264
01:18:00.080 --> 01:18:07.760
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: disbursement rate of 92.6 percent in the last seven years the cfo has maintained more than a 90

asr-000265
01:18:07.760 --> 01:18:15.600
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: disbursement rate. In 2027, the CFO will not only maintain its regular programs such as BaLinkBayan,

asr-000266
01:18:15.600 --> 01:18:22.400
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: YouLeaD, Ugnayan, but also intensify campaigns for further diaspora engagement for national development.

asr-000267
01:18:23.040 --> 01:18:26.560
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: we plan to conduct outreach to overseas filipino organizations

asr-000268
01:18:27.280 --> 01:18:33.120
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: create development focus modules for the youth intensify our anti-human trafficking efforts

asr-000269
01:18:33.120 --> 01:18:36.640
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: and bolster partnerships with other migration and development stakeholders

asr-000270
01:18:37.440 --> 01:18:44.160
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: to help achieve our new goals we are also requesting an additional 88 million 764 000

asr-000271
01:18:44.800 --> 01:18:52.400
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: for the cfo mismo baling buy-in project continuing cost office productivity and our newly created for

asr-000272
01:18:52.400 --> 01:18:58.240
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: filipino diaspora volunteer program supporting the cfo means strengthening our commitment to

asr-000273
01:18:58.240 --> 01:19:04.800
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: every filipino whether they are at home or abroad so with your permission mr chairman i now show

asr-000274
01:19:04.800 --> 01:19:08.800
CFO Chairperson Dante Francis M. Ang II: a brief video to summarize all of these proposals

asr-000275
01:19:32.190 --> 01:19:45.120
Presentation video: Around the world, millions of Filipinos have built lives, careers, and communities. With them is a vast reservoir of knowledge, expertise, networks, resources, and a continuing desire to contribute to the Philippines.

asr-000276
01:19:45.120 --> 01:19:47.240
Presentation video: For many, the question is

asr-000277
01:19:47.240 --> 01:19:48.240
Presentation video: not whether

asr-000278
01:19:48.240 --> 01:19:49.200
Presentation video: they want to help,

asr-000279
01:19:49.200 --> 01:19:50.200
Presentation video: but how, where,

asr-000280
01:19:50.200 --> 01:19:51.280
Presentation video: and with whom

asr-000281
01:19:51.280 --> 01:19:52.320
Presentation video: they can make a meaningful contribution.

asr-000282
01:19:52.320 --> 01:19:55.860
Presentation video: This is where the Commission on Filipinos Overseas, or CFO, comes in.

asr-000283
01:19:56.220 --> 01:20:03.500
Presentation video: CFO connects Filipinos overseas with credible programs, communities, government institutions, and partners

asr-000284
01:20:03.500 --> 01:20:07.400
Presentation video: through which they can remain engaged and contribute to the country's development.

asr-000285
01:20:07.400 --> 01:20:12.540
Presentation video: Around 6 million non-resident Filipinos or NRFs live across the world

asr-000286
01:20:12.540 --> 01:20:19.120
Presentation video: as permanent residents, naturalized and dual citizens, spouses and partners of foreign nationals,

asr-000287
01:20:19.120 --> 01:20:25.660
Presentation video: descendants of Filipino migrants, exchange visitors, and other migrants under the Commission's mandate.

asr-000288
01:20:26.180 --> 01:20:31.120
Presentation video: Across countries, citizenships, and generations, one bond endures.

asr-000289
01:20:31.460 --> 01:20:32.160
Presentation video: Dugong Pinoy

asr-000290
01:20:32.160 --> 01:20:39.200
Presentation video: CFO strengthens the political, economic, and cultural ties of Filipinos overseas with the Philippines

asr-000291
01:20:39.200 --> 01:20:43.700
Presentation video: and facilitates their meaningful participation in national development.

asr-000292
01:20:43.700 --> 01:20:48.840
Presentation video: For Filipinos overseas who want to remain connected and contribute to the Philippines,

asr-000293
01:20:49.120 --> 01:20:51.880
Presentation video: CFO provides concrete ways to take part.

asr-000294
01:20:52.260 --> 01:20:57.420
Presentation video: LINKAPIL connects NRFs who want to give back with channels for supporting local development.

asr-000295
01:20:57.780 --> 01:21:06.820
Presentation video: In 2025, the program facilitated 14.4 million pesos in donations from 2,835 overseas donors,

asr-000296
01:21:07.380 --> 01:21:14.500
Presentation video: benefiting 17,698 Filipinos in 17 provinces and the National Capital Region.

asr-000297
01:21:14.500 --> 01:21:18.300
Presentation video: Beyond immediate assistance, CFO encourages contributions

asr-000298
01:21:18.300 --> 01:21:19.100
Presentation video: that address

asr-000299
01:21:19.120 --> 01:21:21.120
Presentation video: longer-term development needs

asr-000300
01:21:21.120 --> 01:21:23.380
Presentation video: and strengthen community resilience,

asr-000301
01:21:23.720 --> 01:21:26.860
Presentation video: turning bayanihan across borders into concrete action.

asr-000302
01:21:27.100 --> 01:21:27.880
Presentation video: BaLinkBayan

asr-000303
01:21:27.880 --> 01:21:31.760
Presentation video: reconnects Filipinos overseas with their places of origin,

asr-000304
01:21:32.140 --> 01:21:37.920
Presentation video: working with LGUs to link diaspora investments, expertise, community initiatives,

asr-000305
01:21:38.300 --> 01:21:42.020
Presentation video: and other forms of participation with local development needs.

asr-000306
01:21:42.460 --> 01:21:47.580
Presentation video: CFO also engages succeeding generations through Philippine schools overseas,

asr-000307
01:21:48.060 --> 01:21:48.660
Presentation video: YouLeaD,

asr-000310
01:21:49.100 --> 01:21:54.620
Presentation video: and the Virtual Centro Rizal, strengthening Filipino identity and their connection to the homeland.

asr-000311
01:21:54.620 --> 01:22:03.720
Presentation video: Ugnayan brings CFO services, programs, and diaspora engagement initiatives directly to Filipino communities overseas.

asr-000312
01:22:04.140 --> 01:22:07.820
Presentation video: CFO also brings NRF perspectives into policymaking,

asr-000313
01:22:08.380 --> 01:22:14.300
Presentation video: helping ensure that diaspora concerns are reflected in government policy and migration governance.

asr-000314
01:22:14.300 --> 01:22:25.720
Presentation video: PESO Sense strengthens financial literacy, supported by a digital community of 3.9 million followers and nearly 800,000 SAVERS Group members.

asr-000315
01:22:25.940 --> 01:22:31.540
Presentation video: Together, these programs represent one of CFO's defining roles, our second frontline,

asr-000316
01:22:31.840 --> 01:22:35.720
Presentation video: which continues after Filipinos have established lives overseas.

asr-000317
01:22:35.720 --> 01:22:44.080
Presentation video: Here, CFO helps reconnect the diaspora with the Philippines and channel their knowledge, skills, networks, investments,

asr-000318
01:22:44.620 --> 01:22:48.920
Presentation video: philanthropy, and other resources toward national and local development.

asr-000319
01:22:49.280 --> 01:22:54.220
Presentation video: In this way, migration becomes a continuing circulation of knowledge and resources,

asr-000320
01:22:54.620 --> 01:22:59.060
Presentation video: helping transform brain drain into brain gain through diaspora engagement.

asr-000321
01:22:59.380 --> 01:23:02.000
Presentation video: CFO's work also begins before migration.

asr-000322
01:23:02.000 --> 01:23:07.840
Presentation video: At our first frontline, we prepare and support Filipinos as they build new lives overseas.

asr-000323
01:23:08.200 --> 01:23:14.060
Presentation video: In 2025, CFO served 81,859 Filipino migrants,

asr-000324
01:23:14.060 --> 01:23:21.060
Presentation video: and program participants across its pre-departure, counseling, au pair, and exchange visitor programs.

asr-000325
01:23:21.060 --> 01:23:29.740
Presentation video: CFO also protects migrants through the 1343 Action Line and its advocacy and coordination work against trafficking in persons.

asr-000326
01:23:30.220 --> 01:23:35.860
Presentation video: As migration continues to evolve, so must the way government reaches and engages Filipinos overseas.

asr-000327
01:23:36.380 --> 01:23:43.480
Presentation video: CFO is strengthening its digital services, BaLinkBayan, critical information systems, and overseas reach

asr-000328
01:23:43.480 --> 01:23:44.040
Presentation video: through

asr-000329
01:23:44.060 --> 01:23:48.060
Presentation video: honorary diaspora representatives in selected communities.

asr-000330
01:23:48.060 --> 01:23:56.820
Presentation video: These initiatives will make government services more accessible and enable more Filipinos abroad to connect, participate, and contribute to the Philippines.

asr-000331
01:23:56.820 --> 01:24:00.180
Presentation video: As the Filipino diaspora continues to grow and evolve,

asr-000332
01:24:00.180 --> 01:24:05.780
Presentation video: so does the importance of keeping the Philippines connected to Filipinos wherever they may be.

asr-000333
01:24:05.780 --> 01:24:11.380
Presentation video: CFO brings the global Filipino community closer to the country's development needs,

asr-000334
01:24:11.380 --> 01:24:14.060
Presentation video: and brings credible avenues for participation,

asr-000335
01:24:14.060 --> 01:24:17.060
Presentation video: closer to Filipinos wherever they are.

asr-000336
01:24:17.060 --> 01:24:23.060
Presentation video: CFO translates public resources into programs and services for Filipinos overseas.

asr-000337
01:24:23.060 --> 01:24:32.060
Presentation video: In 2025, the Commission posted a 91.36% obligation rate and a 92.60% disbursement rate.

asr-000338
01:24:32.060 --> 01:24:42.060
Presentation video: For Fiscal Year 2027, the CFO has a proposed budget of P195.2 million under the National Expenditure Program.

asr-000339
01:24:42.060 --> 01:24:43.060
Presentation video: Additional resources

asr-000340
01:24:44.060 --> 01:24:48.060
Presentation video: will allow CFO to reach more Filipinos overseas,

asr-000341
01:24:48.060 --> 01:24:50.060
Presentation video: strengthen program delivery,

asr-000342
01:24:50.060 --> 01:24:52.060
Presentation video: expand digital access,

asr-000343
01:24:52.060 --> 01:24:56.060
Presentation video: and deepen diaspora engagement for national and local development.

asr-000344
01:25:00.060 --> 01:25:01.060
